  "body": "U1 of #3663: the tool library leaves the dock and opens in its own window.\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library_dialog/mod.rs`: `tool_library_window(ctx, state)`. It is a non-modal in-app `egui::Window` with the id `tool-library` and the title \"Tool library\". It follows the pattern of the tool shape window. It opens left of the Properties pane, so the user can use the two at the same time.\n- New `tool_library_dialog/list.rs`: the tools list. The body of `egui_app/tool_library.rs` moved here, and that file is deleted. The labels \"Tool type\", \"Name filter\", \"New tool…\", \"Export library…\", \"Import library…\", \"Import tool holders\" and \"Catalog\" do not change.\n  - Two sources: \"Document\" and \"Catalog\". A new window opens on Document when the document has tools, else on Catalog.\n  - The Document list shows the columns of #3663: T, Tool, Kind, Ø, Flute length, Flutes, Holder, Recipes. \"Edit\" shows the tool in Properties.\n  - The Catalog rows keep their label form and their \"Add\" button.\n  - The Tool type and Name filters apply to the two sources.\n- New `crates/ui/src/state_tool_library_dialog.rs`: `ToolLibraryView { source }` and `ToolSource`. `state.rs` gets one field (`tool_library`), the `mod` line and its `pub use`.\n- `actions::target` with the empty tool name opens the window and keeps `ui_target`. The four doors use it: the ribbon Tools cell, the View menu \"Tool library…\", and the gate route for \"no tool\" and for \"no fitting tool\".\n- `LayoutRequest::ToolLibrary` is removed. `shell.rs` draws the window after the tool shape window. `Tab::Tools` draws nothing.\n- The `Tab::Tools` variant stays, because a saved panel setup can name it. `layout::setups::decode` removes the tab on load. It also removes a float that held only that tab.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3892-tool-library-shell.md`.\n\nCommands: none new. \"Add\" uses `AddTool`. Import uses `ImportTools`. Opening and closing the window is view state, as for the tool shape window. No MCP tool is owed.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The window opens at 20 % of the screen width and 15 % of its height, at 620 × (70 % of the screen height). At 1280 × 720 it does not touch the Properties leaf (pinned).\n- `#[test]` count of `crates/ui`: 1768 on `origin/main`, 1770 on this head. One test moved (`layout_page_tool_library` is now `layout_window_tool_library`). Two tests are new.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::page_layout_tool_library::layout_window_tool_library` (new file; `page_layout.rs` is full): the window is open after a click on Tools, its anchors stack top to bottom, and it does not cover Properties.\n- `egui_app::tests::page_layout_tool_library::the_tool_library_window_closes_and_opens_again`.\n- `egui_app::tests::panel_setups::a_saved_setup_with_the_old_tool_library_tab_still_loads`.\n- I ran the first and the third test red on the test-only commit `0604ed8f8` before the change (2 failed: the window was not open; the old tab stayed in the dock).\n\nTests updated, none deleted:\n- `tool_properties::tools_ribbon_opens_the_tool_library_window_without_retargeting_properties` (was `..._opens_a_docked_catalog_...`).\n- `tool_properties::browser_library_door_opens_the_window_and_tool_selection_focuses_properties` (was `..._focus_their_own_dock_tabs`). The window now stays open when a tool is selected.\n- `tool_icon_wiring::every_catalog_row_paints_its_kind_glyph`: it selects the Catalog source first.\n- `gate_route_tests::no_tool_routes_to_the_tool_library`, the drill gate test in `tests.rs`, `panel_setups::arrange` (the float holds Debug info now), the header of `page_layout.rs`, and the Gate maps of `catalog_filters.rs` and `edm_tool_visibility.rs`.\n\n## Gate (Windows, host winbuild, head `be7168455`)\n\nThe Mac build lane belongs to a different agent. All builds and tests ran on the Windows machine winbuild, with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1` and `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 18 steps, 18 ok, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 5.2 min. Steps: ui build, ui lib (115 s), and the ui suites boundary, boundary_picks, catalog_render, contour_dxf_sketch, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files, waterjet_tool. The plan is larger than 10 steps because `state.rs` and `actions.rs` reach more ui suites. The issue expected 10 to about 20.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`): not run. Its dry run lists only `camcraft-motion` and `camcraft-app` twins, and this diff touches `crates/ui` only.\n- No heavy lane (not a `P1`).\n- The example catalog suites: not run. No post or toolpath changed.\n- No snapshot PNG changed. The release-lane pixel snapshots of the shell do not open the tool library, so I expect no change there. They run at the cut.\n- I did not test the window by hand in the native app. The screenshots below come from the egui_kittest harness.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nRendered with the egui_kittest harness (seeded demo document, 1280 × 720) in a scratch test that is not in this PR.\n\nBefore (`origin/main`): the Tools cell opens a dock tab beside Properties.\n\n![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/54de0c1299de6cd4700ce30ce8d53848d1a79781/pr-3892/before-tools.png)\n\nAfter: the Tools cell opens the \"Tool library\" window on the Document source. Properties keeps its subject.\n\n![after, Document](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/54de0c1299de6cd4700ce30ce8d53848d1a79781/pr-3892/after-tools.png)\n\nAfter: the Catalog source.\n\n![after, Catalog](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/54de0c1299de6cd4700ce30ce8d53848d1a79781/pr-3892/after-catalog.png)\n\nChangelog: The Tools ribbon cell opens the tool library in its own window, which can stay open beside the viewport. The \"Tool library\" dock tab is gone.\n\nEffort: high (by the plan; the issue has no labels yet).\n\nRefs #3663\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3892\n",
